module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_parameter_default_value_is_never_judged_against_its_parameter_type

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundBelowTheLadder, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data a_parameter_default_value_is_never_judged_against_its_parameter_type: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_parameter_default_value_is_never_judged_against_its_parameter_type" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundBelowTheLadder, ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "every declared parameter default is judged by the declared-type relation at PositionParameterDefault against the parameter's resolved declared type, refusing a default that does not inhabit it, so a default never reaches the relation with an unresolved formal" } },

  receipts: [
    "**a parameter default reaches the declared-type relation with an UNRESOLVED formal, so it gets the 'formal unresolved' advisory and is never refused** (`fn g(v: Nat = \"x\") -> Nat { v }` compiles: the default is inferred and an obligation is built at PositionParameterDefault, but the relation answers UndecidableFormalUnresolved, an advisory, so nothing refuses a default of the wrong kind and every call that omits the argument receives it). gunbc.compile_clean_diagnostic_policy already classifies this advisory (DeclaredTypeInhabitanceUndecided, 'formal unresolved') as a masked real defect, an unresolvable declared type that should red as UnresolvedType rather than rest as an advisory.",

    "RECEIPT (2026-10-31, sunny-newt-661, srv1, systemd scope RuntimeMaxSec=1800 MemoryMax=16G MemorySwapMax=0). Command: `cd ~/sn-own/src && ~/sn-own/gunbc compile --source-root ~/sn-own/src/dag --entry ~/sn-own/src/dag/test/fixture/sn_dp/p.dag --output-dir ~/sn-own/out2`, entry `module test.fixture.sn_dp.p` IN the layout. Revision: clone ~/sn-own/src HEAD ca41cf39e192e261784e622afd85e199d7a9882b (kh/q1-q2-validation). Binary sha256 f46dc37cd1130c33e5776aca46f6fd2cf15bd92b5567dd256f06e6c3b7341024. Filtered output (`[pre-entry]` lines removed), ~/sn-own/run2.log sha256 b0e8314364059d2ecbe8d1266eb8f8a74697836042728358c1bf31779a379af4; exit 1, 1 blocking, 173 advisory. SPECIMENS: `type Wrap = Wrap { n: Int }`; f `(v: Wrap = 3)`, g `(v: Nat = \"x\")`, h `(v: Wrap = Wrap { n: \"x\" })`: each prints only the advisory 'declared-type inhabitance is undecidable at the parameter default (formal unresolved: the declared type did not resolve to a declaration ...)' and no error. CONTROL, same file and branch: k `(v: Nat = Wrap { n: \"x\" }) -> Nat { \"x\" }`: its BODY `\"x\"` at Nat refuses ('type mismatch: expected Primitive(Nat), got Primitive(String)'), proving the route prints; k's default prints the same advisory. Not established: that the same holds on another binary.",

    "CORRECTION, stated so it is not lost: an earlier version of this row said the default is 'never inferred', from a probe whose entry sat OUTSIDE gunbc.source_layout's governed roots (dag, src/v2) and printed no diagnostics at all. In the layout the default IS inferred and does reach the relation. The silence was the probe's location, not the compiler.",

    "CAUSE, CONFIRMED BY EXECUTION (2026-10-31, sunny-newt-661): parameter_default_emissions built the obligation's declared node as resolved_type(param_node_type_expr(p)). resolve_param stores the resolved, use-site-rendered type AS the type_expr child, so resolved_type over that child read the child's own absent inference, got error_type with an empty name, and declared_type_inhabitance answered UndecidableFormalUnresolved. The direct-call formal chain (bind_local_func_conformance, ResolvedFormal.declared_type) reads param_node_type_expr(p) as-is. Repair at 06ed507844a0a5c805520bcd1a12161ee7d5ee33, no new rule, carried to main by this change as the same parameter_default_emissions text; evidence run3.log sha256 d09c3aeb67729e2b98c7580981782766382bb72cef19033941797037bc431cca, witness log wit.log sha256 ca1abe00956bd5bfe532b74d55d96d4b79c3d1a68b4af7fb83303534c4291217, taken on the q1 stack and to be re-taken on this change's head against main Executed on a fresh clone of that head with the regenerated stage0 mirror, binary sha256 20fdf46a4747734539299787cb35af0ee02fdca6064b62b4ce605d28379beae5: the sn_dp fixture prints ZERO 'formal unresolved' and refuses f (Int at Wrap), g (String at Nat), h (String at the Int field) and k's body; parameter_default_at_declared_type_witness passes 5 of 5. Before the repair, binary f46dc37c on the same fixture refused none of f/g/h.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the capability is met by this change's repair; the rung is read at the ceiling only after it executes on THIS base (main plus this change), not on the q1 stack where it was first run. RED: g and h above, refused after the repair; positive control: the `3` at Nat default and a well-formed record default are accepted.",

    "SECOND TRIGGER, stated so it is not a silent gap: parameter_default_emissions keeps only the default's DIAGNOSTICS; the typed default is not stored back on the param node and emission still reads the untyped default, so a literal introduced at its carrier (Q1b E1b) does not yet reach an emitted default. Visibility is module scope only: stage0 call_function_inner evaluates a default in the caller-supplied env, and v1.compiler.emit_rust fill_default_args / fill_op_default_args splice it at the call site; neither binds a sibling parameter.",

    "SIBLING FINDING (Q1b step 2, not this row's fix): String at std.nat Nat reaches declared_type_inhabitance's terminal UnmodeledNoArmDecides, wrong code the RELATION itself should refuse; the kernel-at-structured arm exempts grounded carriers by design. Hypothesis from reading, to be confirmed by the pre-fix probe. The relation fix belongs to Q1b, not to the default position.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
